  "note": "Golden output of clipBelowPlane. Regenerated 2026-11-13 because the mesh it clips changed: autoOrientToZUp stopped rotating the hull 180 degrees about Z (the bow/stern volume-centroid flip was removed — see the comment at the end of autoOrientToZUp in src/lib/geometry.ts and verify-orientation section 1), which flips every triangle in the mesh this fixture clips. Every digest moved, and the heel-12 heights moved with it. The recipe is unchanged: orient + centre + decimate tests/test-kayak.stl to 12000 tris, then clip per case below. Case kinds: 'midpoint' — 20 heights minZ + (maxZ-minZ)*(k+0.5)/20 over k=0..19; 'vertexZ' — the height is exactly a vertex z of the rolled mesh (quantiles 0.05/0.35/0.65/0.95 of the sorted unique vertex z values), so h - az is exactly 0 for that vertex and every EPS comparison takes its boundary value; 'extremeZ' — h = minZ and h = maxZ; 'degenerate' — h = (minZ + maxZ)/2, the mesh plus two near-degenerate vertical slivers at x=5000 (vertices (5000, 0, -2000), (5000, d, -2000), (5000, d, 2000) with d = 2e-13 and 3e-13), whose cross-product magnitude |d|*4000 is ~8e-10 mm^2 and ~1.2e-9 mm^2 (as float32), one either side of the 1e-9 mm^2 degenerate-triangle reject threshold. Heel 12 deg is applyRollX about the bounds centre y/z. Each case may carry extraTris: flat xyz triples appended to the rolled mesh, in the recorded order. Every expected number came from the current clipper in src/lib/hydrostatics.ts, blob e7d4cf2d98f0b997aef7b46ab64b851598924ffb (commit f56bd7d plus comment-only edits — numbers are unaffected by comments). The generator itself is not kept in the repo; rebuild it from this note.",
